# Supabase

## Migrations are append-only

Never edit a migration that has already run anywhere. Write a new one. Editing in
place is how two machines end up with silently different schemas and a bug nobody
can reproduce.

## RLS is the security boundary, not the app

The anon key ships inside the app binary, so treat every client as hostile. Any
row a policy permits will eventually be read by someone it wasn't meant for.

- Every new table gets `enable row level security` in the same migration that
  creates it. A table with RLS off is readable by anyone holding the anon key.
- Write `(select auth.uid())`, not bare `auth.uid()`, so Postgres evaluates it
  once per query instead of once per row.
- Every policy needs a test proving the owner can *and* a stranger cannot. An
  untested policy is an unproven one.

## Functions

- `security invoker` unless there is a written reason for `definer`.
- Always `set search_path = ''` and schema-qualify every reference. Without it, a
  user-created schema can hijack name resolution inside a definer function.
- Edge functions validate and normalize input before it reaches the database.
